Z||000008||kinboyatuwo||10-29-2001||01:56 PM||||Throw it in second before you go in reverse, has worked for me for the last couple years when that started!<P>kin<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/b4lower50.jpg"> <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||4
Z||000009||Carrolles||10-30-2001||10:44 AM||||My 85SE v-6 4spd does this.  I've just learned to ease it into reverse to let the rotating parts syncronize themselves.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tigger||10-30-2001||10:55 AM||||Yep, mine does it sometimes, 4 spd.  A friend's '79 mustang does the same thing.  I've gotten the habit with the clutch in, putting it back in 1st or 2nd and then R.<P>Waa Hoo, No grindage!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
